{"id":"twitter:1882276301865988108","tweet_id":"1882276301865988108","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1882276301865988108","title":"@JMooreP3 @joni_askola There are controls to help on contentious topics. For example any article about Russia's war in Ukraine and you need to have ma","summary":"@JMooreP3 @joni_askola There are controls to help on contentious topics. For example any article about Russia's war in Ukraine and you need to have made 500 edits. This helps But Wikipedia is very high in the Disinfo Shrill Chain. State actors and PR Firms a general PITA.","date":"2025-01-23","published":"2025-01-23T03:56:56+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/JMooreP3/status/1882205285495771397","reply_tweet_id":"1882205285495771397","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@JMooreP3 @joni_askola There are controls to help on contentious topics. For example any article about Russia&#x27;s war in Ukraine and you need to have made 500 edits. This helps<br><br>But Wikipedia is very high in the Disinfo Shrill Chain. State actors and PR Firms a general PITA.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1882276301865988108","display_date":"January 23, 2025 · 03:56 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1882275661815173312","tweet_id":"1882275661815173312","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1882275661815173312","title":"@teachmonkey2fly @ras_twit2K @joni_askola Wikipedia uses a secondary source rule. So it doesn't make sense to be the greatest fact checking tool if yo","summary":"@teachmonkey2fly @ras_twit2K @joni_askola Wikipedia uses a secondary source rule. So it doesn't make sense to be the greatest fact checking tool if you want primary documents. You cite secondary sources, and most editors rely on the Press. It is hard to make the Deprecated Sources list.","date":"2025-01-23","published":"2025-01-23T03:54:23+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/teachmonkey2fly/status/1882179917246587254","reply_tweet_id":"1882179917246587254","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@teachmonkey2fly @ras_twit2K @joni_askola Wikipedia uses a secondary source rule. So it doesn&#x27;t make sense to be the greatest fact checking tool if you want primary documents.<br><br>You cite secondary sources, and most editors rely on the Press.<br><br>It is hard to make the Deprecated Sources list.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1882275661815173312","display_date":"January 23, 2025 · 03:54 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
