{"id":"twitter:1880349100153139292","tweet_id":"1880349100153139292","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1880349100153139292","title":"As Nation-states emerged in Europe birch got associated with \"White\" as a beauty standard and royalty in German and russian aristocracy (banged a lot)","summary":"As Nation-states emerged in Europe birch got associated with \"White\" as a beauty standard and royalty in German and russian aristocracy (banged a lot) Tribes in Siberia took legends of Birch when pushed out of Northern Europe, to them Birch is a bad omen, white face is coming","date":"2025-01-17","published":"2025-01-17T20:18:55+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1880348195798290733","reply_tweet_id":"1880348195798290733","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>As Nation-states emerged in Europe birch got associated with &quot;White&quot; as a beauty standard and royalty in German and russian aristocracy (banged a lot)<br><br> Tribes in Siberia took legends of Birch when pushed out of Northern Europe, to them Birch is a bad omen, white face is coming</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1880349100153139292","display_date":"January 17, 2025 · 20:18 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1880348195798290733","tweet_id":"1880348195798290733","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1880348195798290733","title":"That Christmas Tree you hang every year...Yeah the entire Pine Tree....that's a North American thing really OG it was Birch and it was hung in the mon","summary":"That Christmas Tree you hang every year...Yeah the entire Pine Tree....that's a North American thing really OG it was Birch and it was hung in the month of Berezozol ..our now April Some say Berezanka river in Ukraine has etymological history with \"Birch\"","date":"2025-01-17","published":"2025-01-17T20:15:19+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1880347486411423950","reply_tweet_id":"1880347486411423950","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>That Christmas Tree you hang every year...Yeah the entire Pine Tree....that&#x27;s a North American thing really<br><br>OG it was Birch and it was hung in the month of Berezozol ..our now April<br><br>Some say Berezanka river in Ukraine has etymological history with &quot;Birch&quot;</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1880348195798290733","display_date":"January 17, 2025 · 20:15 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1880347486411423950","tweet_id":"1880347486411423950","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1880347486411423950","title":"Birch was celebrated and important to the tribes of Western and Eastern Europe and the cultural value has made it's way into folklore written well aft","summary":"Birch was celebrated and important to the tribes of Western and Eastern Europe and the cultural value has made it's way into folklore written well after Christianization. It is in name places all over Europe and surnames like Berezovsky Birch = fertility and protection","date":"2025-01-17","published":"2025-01-17T20:12:30+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1880346402024575183","reply_tweet_id":"1880346402024575183","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Birch was celebrated and important to the tribes of Western and Eastern Europe and the cultural value has made it&#x27;s way into folklore written well after Christianization.<br><br>It is in name places all over Europe and surnames like Berezovsky<br><br>Birch = fertility and protection</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1880347486411423950","display_date":"January 17, 2025 · 20:12 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1880346402024575183","tweet_id":"1880346402024575183","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1880346402024575183","title":"English word Birch comes from Proto-Germanic berkjon From PIE *bhergo which on other branches is Ossetian- barz, Old Church Slavonic- breza, Russian- ","summary":"English word Birch comes from Proto-Germanic berkjon From PIE *bhergo which on other branches is Ossetian- barz, Old Church Slavonic- breza, Russian- bereza Many believe Slavic Goddess Bereginya (russian), Berehynia (Ukraine) draw an etymology from \"birch others \"river bank\"","date":"2025-01-17","published":"2025-01-17T20:08:12+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1880342784911274114","reply_tweet_id":"1880342784911274114","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>English word Birch comes from Proto-Germanic berkjon <br><br>From PIE *bhergo which on other branches is Ossetian- barz, Old Church Slavonic- breza, Russian- bereza<br><br>Many believe  Slavic Goddess Bereginya (russian), Berehynia (Ukraine) draw an etymology from &quot;birch others &quot;river bank&quot;</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1880346402024575183","display_date":"January 17, 2025 · 20:08 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1880342784911274114","tweet_id":"1880342784911274114","source":"twitter","type":"photos","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1880342784911274114","title":"Intertextual collisions After learning about Birch Tree in Slavic religions, russian, Ugro-Finnic, Chukchi, and Khanty peoples I am looking at Kateryn","summary":"Intertextual collisions After learning about Birch Tree in Slavic religions, russian, Ugro-Finnic, Chukchi, and Khanty peoples I am looking at Kateryna Bilokur's \"Flowers and Birch Trees\" differently. Seeing too much meaning in beauty, but that's why it's there https://t.co/spimrXMKnU","date":"2025-01-17","published":"2025-01-17T19:53:49+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Intertextual collisions<br><br>After  learning about Birch Tree in Slavic religions, russian, Ugro-Finnic, Chukchi,  and Khanty peoples I am looking at Kateryna Bilokur&#x27;s &quot;Flowers and Birch Trees&quot; differently.<br><br>Seeing too much meaning in beauty, but that&#x27;s why it&#x27;s there <a href=\"https://t.co/spimrXMKnU\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/spimrXMKnU</a></p><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/01fe1c380ddc3a528db66a83a35a9684.jpg\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1880342784911274114","display_date":"January 17, 2025 · 19:53 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":["/archive/twitter/media/01fe1c380ddc3a528db66a83a35a9684.jpg"]}
