{"id":"twitter:1879602644551119046","tweet_id":"1879602644551119046","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1879602644551119046","title":"@TheJellyMan @AnnaOdesitka @smackm8 \"In Russian folk legends, the Chuds were described as exalted and beautiful. One characteristic of the Chuds was '","summary":"@TheJellyMan @AnnaOdesitka @smackm8 \"In Russian folk legends, the Chuds were described as exalted and beautiful. One characteristic of the Chuds was 'white-eyed', which means lightly colored eyes.\" How they draw Chud's in American folklore https://t.co/rnYMMCYvD2","date":"2025-01-15","published":"2025-01-15T18:52:46+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1879602231454142777","reply_tweet_id":"1879602231454142777","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@TheJellyMan @AnnaOdesitka @smackm8 &quot;In Russian folk legends,  the Chuds were described as exalted and beautiful. One characteristic  of the Chuds was &#x27;white-eyed&#x27;, which means lightly colored eyes.&quot;<br><br>How they draw Chud&#x27;s in American folklore <a href=\"https://t.co/rnYMMCYvD2\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/rnYMMCYvD2</a></p><p><a href=\"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1879602644551119046\">Watch the video in the original tweet</a></p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1879602644551119046","display_date":"January 15, 2025 · 18:52 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1879602231454142777","tweet_id":"1879602231454142777","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1879602231454142777","title":"@TheJellyMan @AnnaOdesitka @smackm8 ......Arguably, the earliest attested written use of the word \"Chuds\" to describe Baltic Finnic peoples (presumabl","summary":"@TheJellyMan @AnnaOdesitka @smackm8 ......Arguably, the earliest attested written use of the word \"Chuds\" to describe Baltic Finnic peoples (presumably early Estonians) was c. 1100, in the earliest Rus' chronicles in the Old East Slavic language..... I was this many years old when I learned that","date":"2025-01-15","published":"2025-01-15T18:51:07+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1879602075728035926","reply_tweet_id":"1879602075728035926","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@TheJellyMan @AnnaOdesitka @smackm8 ......Arguably, the earliest attested written use of the word &quot;Chuds&quot; to describe Baltic Finnic peoples (presumably early Estonians) was c. 1100, in the earliest Rus&#x27; chronicles in the Old East Slavic language.....<br><br>I was this many years old when I learned that</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1879602231454142777","display_date":"January 15, 2025 · 18:51 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
