{"id":"twitter:1878445878899257818","tweet_id":"1878445878899257818","source":"twitter","type":"notes","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1878445878899257818","title":"Under New York law it is not a misdemeanor, but a felony, if the fraud may have been used as part of an underlying crime. Probably no first time non-v","summary":"Under New York law it is not a misdemeanor, but a felony, if the fraud may have been used as part of an underlying crime. Probably no first time non-violent offender would see jail time for the felony conviction. https://x.com/ByronYork/status/1878427843849318461","date":"2025-01-12","published":"2025-01-12T14:16:12+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Under New York law it is not a misdemeanor, but a felony, if the fraud may have been used as part of an underlying crime.<br><br>Probably no first time non-violent offender would see jail time for the felony conviction. <a href=\"https://x.com/ByronYork/status/1878427843849318461\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://x.com/ByronYork/status/1878427843849318461</a></p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1878445878899257818","display_date":"January 12, 2025 · 14:16 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
