{"id":"twitter:1873814088566136903","tweet_id":"1873814088566136903","source":"twitter","type":"notes","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1873814088566136903","title":"\"Alternate theory\" and \"Alternative theory\" usage really confuse. https://www.etymonline.com/search?q=alternate and I have never had an editor call me","summary":"\"Alternate theory\" and \"Alternative theory\" usage really confuse. https://www.etymonline.com/search?q=alternate and I have never had an editor call me out for using one incorrectly An alternate reality is an \"other,\" choice. Alternative reality is choosing between two versions in the multiverse","date":"2024-12-30","published":"2024-12-30T19:31:07+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>&quot;Alternate theory&quot;  and &quot;Alternative theory&quot; usage really confuse.<br><br><a href=\"https://www.etymonline.com/search?q=alternate\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://www.etymonline.com/search?q=alternate</a><br><br>and I have never had an editor call me out for using one incorrectly<br><br>An alternate reality is an &quot;other,&quot; choice. Alternative reality is choosing between two versions in the multiverse</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1873814088566136903","display_date":"December 30, 2024 · 19:31 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
